      "message": "There is also a very old bug related to this.\n\nAlso, this is theoretically a breaking change (people _may_ hold packages as open, and in some cases that is actually correct), so we _may_ want to gate this change on the language version. not sure.\n\nOverall, this needs a lot more tests. Consider the following:\n\nimport \".../cli\"\n\na: cli\nb: a.MkDir // will this catch it? Should it.\n\nb: {try { cli.Mkdir? }} // should this fail (I think it will). Should it?\n\u003d\u003d\u003d\npackage cli\n\nx: y: z: {}\n\n---\nimport \"cli\"\n\na: cli.x.y.Z // will this be caught (I think not). Should it?\n\n---\na: {try { cli.x.y.Z? }} // should this fail? If so, why?",
